    "created_at": "2023-06-29T10:49:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-29T10:49:09Z",
    "body": "I think it is due to another sh being sourced that potentially modify the `PROMPT_COMMAND` variable. In my case it was due to `source /usr/share/autojump/autojump.sh` which inside change the `PROMPT_COMMAND`. \r\nChanging the order of initialization in the .bashrc can make it work (had to put this line before starship init) but might have an impact on autojump https://github.com/wting/autojump#known-issues.\r\n\r\nIt would be nice if starship was resilient to the order in the .bashrc without impacting commands that need to set `PROMPT_COMMAND` (not sure it if it is possible).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
