    "created_at": "2023-11-19T09:13:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-11-19T09:38:45Z",
    "body": "> Disabling kitty shell integration solves the problem.\r\n\r\nYou don't have to disable all of it - use the `no-rc` option. I'm currently trying to debug the issue, and found `no-rc` to work. [Kitty's integration configuration docs](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/shell-integration/#configuration)\r\n\r\nEdit: Kitty does modify `PROMPT_COMMAND` when doing the rc integration - specifically in file `$KITTY_INSTALLATION_DIR/shell-integration/bash/kitty.bash`\r\n\r\nEdit 2: I have come up with something that looks like a fix/workaround, but not sure how that impacts the actual rc integration from kitty.\r\n- disable rc integration in kitty.conf\r\n- using the [manual integration](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/shell-integration/#manual-shell-integration), add the relevant code in your .rc files BEFORE starship's init eval",
    "author_association": "NONE",
